DESIGN DECISIONS
- confirmed_at gates claimability. Pending rows appear with their
  confidence score and are excluded from the total, with the count of
  those awaiting confirmation shown next to it. The figure feeding a
  return is never one only a model has seen.
- An edited figure supersedes the extraction, and the panel shows what was
  extracted alongside it, so a correction is visible AS a correction.
  `extracted` retains the original.
- The rate-schedule estimate is shown only when nothing is uploaded, is
  labelled an estimate, and is excluded from the report. It ignores
  amortisation and offset balances and will not tie to the lender - a
  number that cannot be supported must not look claimable.
- Failed extraction still surfaces the stored document with a prompt to
  type the figure. The evidence is what the pack ships.
- Delete removes the storage object explicitly; storage has no DB cascade.

DEFECT CAUGHT DURING IMPLEMENTATION
The scripted edit that added the interest row to the PDF swapped the two
guards: loan interest rendered under `totalOperatingExpenses > 0` and
operating expenses under `totalLoanInterest > 0`. It compiled cleanly and
type-checked - JSX structure was valid, only the semantics were inverted -
so the build would not have caught it. Found by reading the resulting
block rather than trusting the green build, and corrected before commit.
Worth noting as a limitation of the sole automated gate: a passing tsc
says nothing about whether a condition guards the right element.

